  "value": 25,
  "description": "<iframe src=\"\" style=\"background-image: url('https://deadface.sfo3.cdn.digitaloceanspaces.com/2026/img/wayfinder/demonnebreach.png');background-size:cover;background-position:center center;background-origin:content-box;background-repeat:no-repeat;background-color:rgba(40, 40, 40,0);min-height:80px;height:130px;width:100%;padding:10px;border:none\" title=\"Thumbnail\"></iframe>\r\n<sup>Created By: <code>@syyntax</code></sup>\r\n\r\nDEADFACE managed to slip a rogue Kali device onto De Monne Financial’s corporate network. Shortly afterward, someone used a legitimate employee account to access the company file share and steal sensitive documents.\r\n\r\nOne of those documents later surfaced in Ghost Town, confirming that the breach was more than just suspicious network activity.\r\n\r\nZeroTrace recovered a packet capture and a memory image from the affected environment. Your first task is to identify the De Monne Financial employee account that DEADFACE compromised.\r\n\r\nWhat is the username of the compromised employee? Submit the flag as `deadface{username}`.\r\n\r\n[Download memory.7z](https://deadface.sfo3.cdn.digitaloceanspaces.com/2026/challenges/for/dctf26-for/memory.7z)(~1.3GB zipped; 8.0GB unzipped)<br>\r\n<sup>SHA256: `0eea0842a84240d0f2c9ce3564e250bd5367479b831f7be72247ae3dc43f8524`</sup>",
